  "result": "All existing tests pass with the fix.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was in `indexSitesFixesConfig()` in `src/generators/utils/parse.ts`. The delimiter regex `/\\s*={2,}\\s*/gm` matched any run of `==` (2+ equals signs) anywhere in the text, including inside base64-encoded data URLs embedded in custom CSS (e.g. `...ErkJggg==')`). This caused the parser to incorrectly split a CSS block mid-string, treating text after the base64 padding as the start of a new record \u2014 which then got misinterpreted as a domain pattern and later crashed `createUrlRegex` when compiled as regex.\n\nFixed by anchoring the delimiter regex to match only when `==...` occupies an entire line by itself (as the format intends, e.g. a line of just `====`):\n\n```js\nconst delimiterRegex = /^\\s*={2,}\\s*$/gm;\n```\n\nThis preserves detection of legitimate delimiter lines while no longer matching `==` padding that appears embedded within other content on a line (like a base64 string followed by `')  !important;`).\n\nVerified with the existing test suite (`tests/generators/utils/parse.tests.ts`), all 7 tests pass.",
